Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cmake, libopencv-dev, libpam0g-dev, nlohmann-json3-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/Vladush/LinuxCamPAM

Package: linuxcampam
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libpam0g, systemd, v4l-utils
Recommends: rocm-opencl-runtime | intel-opencl-icd | nvidia-opencl-icd-340 | nvidia-opencl-icd
Description: Face Authentication PAM Module (LinuxCamPAM)
  LinuxCamPAM is a Pluggable Authentication Module (PAM) that provides face
  recognition authentication using OpenCV DNN. Supports GPU acceleration via
  OpenCL on Intel, AMD, and NVIDIA hardware.
  .
  This package installs the PAM module, the authentication service, and the
  necessary machine learning models.
